# Binding: this install's model (ExecPlan 0006 P2)

The install's one binding (STEW `spec/binding.md`; ADR-0019 migration step 5, ADR-0020 decision 3): the model every
call uses, the server it is on, and the options it is loaded with. It is the only place Steward's model is named.
Change the model here, not in code. Another install binds the model its hardware runs; this one binds `steward:1`,
STEW's reference binding (`examples/bindings/steward-gpt-oss-20b.us`). `provides` is what the model offers; a profile
whose `requires` it does not meet is refused with what is missing.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "binding",
  "name": "steward-gpt-oss-20b",
  "api": "ollama",
  "endpoint": "http://127.0.0.1:11434",
  "model": "steward:1",
  "provides": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "context": 65536,
    "structured_output": true,
    "reasoning_effort": true
  },
  "hardware": "one 16 GB GPU",
  "options": {
    "num_ctx": 65536,
    "keep_alive": "30m"
  }
}
```
